1
00:00:02,222 --> 00:00:07,253
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, Madinan Period Volume 2

2
00:00:07,796 --> 00:00:09,910
By Imam Anwar_Awlaki,

3
00:00:10,586 --> 00:00:19,407
اَلْحَمْدُ لله رَبِّ الْعلَمِيْن ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِ الْاَنْبِيَاءِ وَلْمُرْسَلِيْن ، مُحَمَّد اِبْنِ عَبْدالله وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

4
00:00:19,431 --> 00:00:21,211
السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

5
00:00:21,235 --> 00:00:26,427
We're carrying on with the Battle of the conquest of Makkah, Fath Makkah(فتح مكه).

6
00:00:26,957 --> 00:00:29,370
We said that Rasool Allah ﷺ left in Ramadan(رمضان),

7
00:00:29,929 --> 00:00:38,373
and when they were close to Makkah, they started breaking their fast by the command of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

8
00:00:38,484 --> 00:00:40,960
 they were told not to carry on fasting.

9
00:00:41,488 --> 00:00:45,123
They reached an area called Marr Az-Zahran(مرة أظهران) on their way.

10
00:00:45,384 --> 00:00:48,410
And there were trees of Araak(أراك),

11
00:00:48,473 --> 00:00:52,316
Araak(أراك) is the tree which Miswaak(مسواك) is taken from,

12
00:00:52,722 --> 00:00:56,507
the good Miswaak(مسواك) is the root of this tree,

13
00:00:56,912 --> 00:01:02,575
but also the branches, the tender branches can be used as a Miswaak(مسواك).

14
00:01:03,008 --> 00:01:04,755
So, the tree is called Al-Araak(الاراك) .

15
00:01:05,251 --> 00:01:08,623
There's a tiny fruit for this tree called Al-Kubbaas(ألكباث),

16
00:01:09,369 --> 00:01:12,786
very small, like a pea, but smaller than a pea.

17
00:01:12,925 --> 00:01:19,933
And they're sweet, but they also have that taste of Al-Miswaak(مسواك) in them, and they're edible.

18
00:01:20,314 --> 00:01:24,072
 So, the Sahabah(صحابه) were plucking, this Kubbas(الكباث)

19
00:01:24,096 --> 00:01:29,323
and Rasool Allah ﷺ told them to take the black ones because they are the best.

20
00:01:29,763 --> 00:01:35,412
Because it starts out as green and then it turns, I think yellow and red and then and then Black.

21
00:01:35,829 --> 00:01:37,925
So, black is when it's ripe.

22
00:01:38,313 --> 00:01:42,037
Now, Al-Araak(الاراك) doesn't grow in Makkah, it's outside of Makkah.

23
00:01:42,061 --> 00:01:48,392
So, they told Rasool Allah ﷺ, you must have been a shepherd of sheep.

24
00:01:48,865 --> 00:01:53,607
Because it is the shepherd's, who eat Al-Kubbas(الكباث), since it is outside the Makkah,

25
00:01:53,670 --> 00:01:56,548
they're the ones, who usually harvest it, and eat it.

26
00:01:56,881 --> 00:02:01,208
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes, and every Nabbi(نبي) has been a shepherd.

27
00:02:01,442 --> 00:02:03,407
Every Nabbi(نبي) has been a shepherd of sheep.

28
00:02:03,770 --> 00:02:10,107
And we talked about the Hikmah(حكمه), the wisdom behind the Ambiyaa(أنبياء) of Allah being shepherds.

29
00:02:10,167 --> 00:02:13,813
We talked about that, in one of the lectures of Makkah.

30
00:02:14,145 --> 00:02:17,442
Abdullah Bin Masood رضي الله عنه was climbing.

31
00:02:17,727 --> 00:02:21,362
This is not very high tree, it's like a short tree.

32
00:02:21,791 --> 00:02:27,869
So, Abdullah Bin Masood رضي الله عنه was climbing to try to get the Al-Kubbas(الكباث)

33
00:02:28,333 --> 00:02:32,766
and his legs were showing, his shin, they were very, very slim.

34
00:02:33,321 --> 00:02:39,047
So, some of the Sahabah(صحابه) were laughing, at the thinness of his legs.

35
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:40,527
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

36
00:02:40,906 --> 00:02:45,845
You are surprised by the thinness of the shins of Abdullah Bin Masood(عبد الله بن مسعود),

37
00:02:46,149 --> 00:02:51,898
in the name of Allah, they are heavier on the scales, on the Day of Judgment than the mountain of Uhud(أحَد).

38
00:02:52,364 --> 00:02:57,279
So, Abdullah Bin Masood(عبد الله بن مسعود) is going to be very heavy on the scales on the Day of Judgment.

39
00:02:57,514 --> 00:02:59,734
His deeds are very heavy.

40
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:07,115
And Rasool Allah ﷺ, he gave this Fazilah(فضيلة) to Abdullah Bin Masood رضي الله عنه, this virtue.

41
00:03:07,571 --> 00:03:10,230
And when they were walking, suddenly a rabbit jumped.

42
00:03:11,019 --> 00:03:16,657
So, they followed it and one of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم was able to catch the rabbit.

43
00:03:16,845 --> 00:03:19,878
So, they took it to, Abu Talha(ابو طلحه), who slaughtered it

44
00:03:20,295 --> 00:03:24,829
and then they sent a piece of it to Rasool Allah ﷺ, and he ate it.

45
00:03:25,043 --> 00:03:26,763
So, rabbit is Halal(حلال).

46
00:03:27,224 --> 00:03:31,849
Up until that moment, Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) had no idea about the movements of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

47
00:03:32,010 --> 00:03:34,143
A huge army of 10,000 strong,

48
00:03:34,848 --> 00:03:41,939
yet Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were blind and deaf concerning the movements of Rasool Ullah.

49
00:03:42,195 --> 00:03:46,138
While whenever, Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) would make a movement Rasool Allah ﷺ would be alerted.

50
00:03:46,311 --> 00:03:54,057
So, the intelligence gathering of Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Muslims was at a much higher caliber than Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

51
00:03:54,418 --> 00:03:57,250
And that is a blessing from Allahعَزّوجَلّ that

52
00:03:57,274 --> 00:04:00,349
he gave the Muslims even though their resources were much less

53
00:04:00,868 --> 00:04:03,715
and the Kuffar(كفار) in the area were much more.

54
00:04:04,055 --> 00:04:07,380
I mean, the number of Muslims, until that moment was quite small,

55
00:04:07,728 --> 00:04:12,340
was limited to Madina and the surrounding areas of Madina, the rest of Arabia were all Kuffar(كفار).

56
00:04:12,658 --> 00:04:18,997
Nevertheless, Rasool Allah ﷺ had disciplined and trained the Sahabah(صحابه) to be alert

57
00:04:19,068 --> 00:04:23,757
 and he would send them out scouting for information,

58
00:04:24,029 --> 00:04:28,781
while Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) up until, this moment had no clue about what was going on.

59
00:04:29,668 --> 00:04:35,788
Another reason which made the intelligence gathering of the Muslims better than Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

60
00:04:36,062 --> 00:04:41,501
is the loyalty that, they had to Rasool Allah ﷺ, so information would not leak.

61
00:04:41,991 --> 00:04:49,235
And as we have seen in the case of Hatib Ibn Abi Baltaa رضي الله عنه that was a single case,

62
00:04:49,602 --> 00:04:55,613
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was alerted to it, by Al-Wahee(ألوحي).

63
00:04:56,125 --> 00:05:03,581
So, the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم would never disclose information about the movements of the Muslims.

64
00:05:03,994 --> 00:05:06,947
One of the things that we suffer today is the lack of loyalty,

65
00:05:07,357 --> 00:05:09,994
and the lack of understanding of Al-Wala Wal Baraa(ألولآء ولبرآء).

66
00:05:10,139 --> 00:05:19,205
So Muslims who claim to be Muslims are willing not only to give information on a single incident basis,

67
00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:26,433
but are willing to work long term for the Kuffar(كفار) giving them information about the Muslims,

68
00:05:26,609 --> 00:05:29,634
spying against the Muslims, and this is Nifaq(نفاق).

69
00:05:29,927 --> 00:05:31,940
A person, who does so is a Munafiq(منافق).

70
00:05:32,387 --> 00:05:37,527
A person who gives up information about the Muslims, spies in the Masajid(مساجد),

71
00:05:37,925 --> 00:05:40,812
and collects information and delivers it to the Kuffar(كفار).

72
00:05:41,089 --> 00:05:44,398
How will he escape the wrath of Allahعَزّوجَلّ on the day of Judgment?

73
00:05:44,809 --> 00:05:47,652
So, Muslims need to fear Allah, they need to have Taqwa(تقوى)

74
00:05:47,906 --> 00:05:51,575
and they need to have the correct understanding of what Al-Wala Wal Baraa(ألولآء ولبرآء) means.

75
00:05:52,380 --> 00:05:57,190
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was in this area of Marr Az-Zahran(مرة أظهران),

76
00:05:57,421 --> 00:06:01,165
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) himself, the leader of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

77
00:06:01,372 --> 00:06:04,001
along with Budail Bin Warqah(بديل بن ورقع) and Hakeem Bin Hizaam(حكيم بن حزام),

78
00:06:04,373 --> 00:06:09,340
they came out of Makkah, searching for information, asking the travelers.

79
00:06:09,758 --> 00:06:18,307
At night they were close to the Muslim army and they saw the lights of the Muslims.

80
00:06:18,780 --> 00:06:20,862
So, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) is saying, who are these?

81
00:06:21,389 --> 00:06:24,438
Budail Bin Warqah(بديل بن ورقع) said: This is Khuza'a(خزاعه) preparing for war.

82
00:06:24,622 --> 00:06:30,426
Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) said: Khuza'a(خزاعه) is much less than this, to have all of these lights.

83
00:06:30,736 --> 00:06:32,154
This cannot be Khuza'a(خزاعه)

84
00:06:32,588 --> 00:06:33,567
اَظلُّ أقل

85
00:06:33,591 --> 00:06:39,912
He said: They are more humble and few, to have these lights.

86
00:06:40,916 --> 00:06:47,795
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) and Budail(بديل) and Hakeem(حكيم) were overseeing the Muslim army

87
00:06:48,291 --> 00:06:54,591
but the Muslim guards were alert and they arrested the three of them.

88
00:06:55,072 --> 00:06:56,762
And they took them to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

89
00:06:56,794 --> 00:06:59,778
in one narration, they were arrested and that's a stronger narration.

90
00:06:59,816 --> 00:07:03,686
In another narration, it was Al-Abbas Ibn Abdul Muttalib(العباس اِبن عبد  المطلب), who found them.

91
00:07:03,934 --> 00:07:06,944
Anyway, we'll go with the narration that, they were arrested

92
00:07:07,024 --> 00:07:09,858
 so they were taken to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

93
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:16,115
In one narration it says, that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) saw Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان),

94
00:07:16,711 --> 00:07:17,950
so he wanted to kill him.

95
00:07:18,689 --> 00:07:25,625
But Al-Abbas(العباس) had Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) ride on the mule of Rasool Allah ﷺ

96
00:07:26,191 --> 00:07:31,541
and he was rushing to get to Rasool Allah ﷺ before Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) can kill Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان),

97
00:07:31,905 --> 00:07:36,218
until they entered into the place where Rasool Allah ﷺ was

98
00:07:36,535 --> 00:07:40,640
and Umar(عمر) tried to have Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) killed.

99
00:07:40,964 --> 00:07:45,209
While Al-Abbas(العباس) was appealing to Rasool Allah ﷺ to spare his life.

100
00:07:45,768 --> 00:07:47,980
And the argument kept on going on,

101
00:07:48,004 --> 00:07:51,343
Al-Abbas(العباس) is trying to convince Rasool Allah ﷺ to spare his life

102
00:07:51,643 --> 00:07:56,049
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is trying to convince Rasool Allah ﷺ to allow him to be executed.

103
00:07:56,315 --> 00:07:58,188
And then Al-Abbas(العباس) got angry and he said;

104
00:07:58,228 --> 00:08:01,567
 O Umar(عمر), if he was one of Bannu Addi(بنوعدي),

105
00:08:01,607 --> 00:08:08,413
Bannu Addi(بنوعدي) are the clan of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) is the tribe and then you have clans.

106
00:08:08,875 --> 00:08:11,253
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) belongs to Bannu Addi(بنوعدي),

107
00:08:11,430 --> 00:08:16,300
so Al-Abbas(العباس) is telling Umar(عمر), if he was from amongst the clan of Bannu Addi(بنوعدي),

108
00:08:16,562 --> 00:08:20,513
you wouldn't have said so, but you know that he is from Abdul Manaf(بنوعبد مناف),

109
00:08:20,537 --> 00:08:23,516
Bannu Abd-Manaf(بنوعبد المناف) are the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ

110
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:27,432
and also the family of Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), they're both descendants of Abd-Manaf(عبد المناف).

111
00:08:28,252 --> 00:08:30,439
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) told Al-Abbas(العباس),

112
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:32,572
مَهْلًا يَا عَبَّاْس

113
00:08:32,879 --> 00:08:34,142
wait, Al-Abbas(العباس)

114
00:08:34,308 --> 00:08:42,451
 your Islam is more beloved to me then the Islam of my father Al-Khattab(الخطاب), if he had became Muslim.

115
00:08:43,026 --> 00:08:50,379
Because I know that Rasool Allah ﷺ would become more pleased by the Islam of you,

116
00:08:50,667 --> 00:08:52,753
then if my father has become Muslim.

117
00:08:52,991 --> 00:08:55,756
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is making it clear to Al-Abbas(العباس) that,

118
00:08:55,780 --> 00:09:00,886
this is not how, we Muslims think we don't think on a tribal level.

119
00:09:01,225 --> 00:09:03,433
That's not our way of thinking.

120
00:09:03,914 --> 00:09:07,226
I am more happy for your Islam

121
00:09:07,428 --> 00:09:11,061
because you are the uncle of Rasool Ullah and it is pleasing to Rasool Ullah,

122
00:09:11,510 --> 00:09:14,667
so what pleases me, is what pleases Rasool Ullah

123
00:09:14,866 --> 00:09:20,298
and what makes me angry is what displeases Rasool Allah ﷺ.

124
00:09:20,702 --> 00:09:27,755
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) here is giving Al-Abbas Ibn Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبد المطلب) a lesson in how the Muslims think.

125
00:09:28,227 --> 00:09:37,646
We do not view things from a nationalistic view, or family based view, or a clan view, or tribal view.

126
00:09:37,966 --> 00:09:40,246
We based things on Al-Wala Wal Baraa(ألولآء ولبرآء),

127
00:09:40,562 --> 00:09:44,847
if a person is close to Allah, then we are loyal to that person.

128
00:09:45,062 --> 00:09:51,435
If a person is far away from Allah, then we are free and we disassociate ourselves from such a person.

129
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:57,699
Anyway Rasool Allah ﷺ told them to leave and come back in the morning, according to that narration,

130
00:09:58,150 --> 00:10:00,688
and when they met in the morning,

131
00:10:00,919 --> 00:10:06,027
Rasool Allah ﷺ accepted the Islam of Budail Bin Warqah(بديل بن ورقع) and Hakeem Bin Hizaam(حكيم بن حزام).

132
00:10:06,356 --> 00:10:08,913
To Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

133
00:10:09,229 --> 00:10:13,375
Isn't it about time, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) that you recognize that there is no god but One.

134
00:10:13,676 --> 00:10:15,878
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) said, to Rasool Allah ﷺ

135
00:10:15,902 --> 00:10:17,568
مَا اَحْلَمَكَ وَمَا اَكْرَمَكْ

136
00:10:17,951 --> 00:10:21,295
You're merciful and you are generous.

137
00:10:21,883 --> 00:10:23,218
And then, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) said;

138
00:10:23,628 --> 00:10:26,222
If there were any other gods besides Allah,

139
00:10:26,246 --> 00:10:28,679
they would have given us protection and have defended us.

140
00:10:28,950 --> 00:10:32,937
So, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) has accepted that there is no God but Allah.

141
00:10:33,441 --> 00:10:35,773
There is no one worthy of worship but Allah, he accepted that.

142
00:10:36,254 --> 00:10:37,936
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told him.

143
00:10:38,269 --> 00:10:43,405
Isn't it about time Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), that you testify that I am the messenger of Allah.

144
00:10:43,621 --> 00:10:49,409
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) said: O Rasool Ullah, there's something in my heart against this at the moment.

145
00:10:49,634 --> 00:10:50,287
So, I accept

146
00:10:50,311 --> 00:10:51,718
اَشْهَدُ الله الهَ الَّا الله

147
00:10:51,988 --> 00:10:57,068
but I still feel difficulty accepting that Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah.

148
00:10:57,282 --> 00:11:00,362
Al-Abbas(العباس) told him: Woe to you, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان),

149
00:11:00,858 --> 00:11:05,510
become a Muslim before your head is chopped, before you're executed,

150
00:11:05,744 --> 00:11:06,645
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) said;

151
00:11:06,669 --> 00:11:08,430
وَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدَ الرَّسُوْل الله

152
00:11:08,685 --> 00:11:09,650
And he became a Muslim.

153
00:11:10,388 --> 00:11:16,132
Rasool Allah ﷺ gave his instructions to Al-Abbas(العباس) to hold back, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) from leaving

154
00:11:16,521 --> 00:11:20,567
 and to have him, wait at the mountain pass.

155
00:11:21,241 --> 00:11:27,177
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted Al-Abbas(العباس) to hold back Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) for a reason.

156
00:11:27,503 --> 00:11:30,437
And he wanted him to wait at the mountain pass for a reason.

157
00:11:30,838 --> 00:11:38,086
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to demonstrate, to the leader of the Kuffar(كفار), the strength of the Muslims.

158
00:11:38,428 --> 00:11:43,257
When Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) would see, the overwhelming forces

159
00:11:43,652 --> 00:11:48,158
that Rasool Allah ﷺ has brought together, to invade Makkah

160
00:11:48,513 --> 00:11:55,571
that would stop and bring an end to any willingness or desire to resist.

161
00:11:56,091 --> 00:11:58,522
Because even though Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) has become Muslim,

162
00:11:58,546 --> 00:12:02,234
he's a new Muslim and he's a leader of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and he might have some interest there,

163
00:12:02,512 --> 00:12:05,362
and the people in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) might want to fight.

164
00:12:05,577 --> 00:12:09,981
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted these people, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) and the ones with him,

165
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:14,288
to see with their own eyes because hearing something is not like seeing it.

166
00:12:14,893 --> 00:12:20,354
To see with their own eyes, the 10,000 strong army of Rasool Allah ﷺ

167
00:12:20,701 --> 00:12:23,807
because Rasool Allah ﷺ did not want bloodshed in Makkah.

168
00:12:24,125 --> 00:12:27,601
So, he wanted them to see, how strong the Muslims are so that they would just surrender.

169
00:12:28,464 --> 00:12:33,192
Rasool Allah ﷺ has divided the army into battalions, you can see.

170
00:12:33,751 --> 00:12:38,411
And every battalion had a Ra'yah(راية), had the banner.

171
00:12:39,204 --> 00:12:43,359
And they were divided according to their tribes.

172
00:12:43,683 --> 00:12:48,739
So, Bannu Sulaim(بنوسُلَيم), were separate, Ghifaar(غفار) were separate, Muzaina(مزينه)

173
00:12:49,321 --> 00:12:54,119
and they were passing from this mountain pass because it's a narrow area,

174
00:12:54,491 --> 00:12:56,648
they were passing one after the other.

175
00:12:56,980 --> 00:13:03,381
And whenever, one of these battalions would move through the mountain pass,

176
00:13:03,682 --> 00:13:06,517
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) would ask Al-Abbas(العباس). Who are they?

177
00:13:06,935 --> 00:13:09,927
And Al-Abbas(العباس) would tell him, this is the Ghifaar(غفار), Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) would say:

178
00:13:09,952 --> 00:13:11,230
مَا لِيْ وَمَا لِلْغِفَار

179
00:13:12,054 --> 00:13:14,770
I have nothing to do with Ghifaar(غفار).

180
00:13:14,970 --> 00:13:17,281
And then Sulaim(سُلَيْم), I have nothing to do with Sulaim(سُلَيْم),

181
00:13:17,799 --> 00:13:21,146
Muzaina(مزينه), I have nothing to do with Muzaina(مزينه).

182
00:13:21,447 --> 00:13:28,515
Until one battalion passed and it caught the attention of Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان).

183
00:13:28,555 --> 00:13:32,637
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), you can sometimes sense the strength of what you see.

184
00:13:33,024 --> 00:13:35,921
So, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) saw this particular battalion

185
00:13:35,969 --> 00:13:38,826
and it caught his attention and he told Al-Abbas(العباس), who are these.?

186
00:13:39,152 --> 00:13:41,203
Al-Abbas(العباس) told him, these are the Al-Ansaar(اَلْاَنْصَار).

187
00:13:41,598 --> 00:13:45,921
And the banner of Al-Ansaar(اَلْاَنْصَار) was with Saad Ibn Ubadah رضي الله عنه,

188
00:13:46,308 --> 00:13:47,723
who was the leader of Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج).

189
00:13:48,181 --> 00:13:52,261
When Sa'ad(سعد) saw, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), he told Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان).

190
00:13:52,285 --> 00:13:56,265
يا أبوسُفِيان اَلْيَوْمْ يَوْمُ الْمَلْحَمَّه، اَلْيَوْمْ تسْتَحَلَ الْكَعْبَهْ

191
00:13:56,550 --> 00:14:03,819
Today is the day of the great battle, today is the day when the sanctuary of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) would be violated.

192
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:10,258
Saad Ibn Ubadah رضي الله عنه, a great Sahabi(صحابي) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, a leader of Al-Ansaar(اَلْاَنْصَار),

193
00:14:10,298 --> 00:14:15,062
 one of the men, who gave Nusrah(نصرة), victory to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

194
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:22,777
however at that particular moment, enthusiasm probably led him to speak out and utter these words.

195
00:14:22,945 --> 00:14:26,808
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) and Al-Abbas(العباس) and others and even says that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب),

196
00:14:27,169 --> 00:14:32,311
they carried these words of Saad Ibn Ubadah(سَعد اِبن عبادة) to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

197
00:14:32,625 --> 00:14:33,761
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

198
00:14:33,785 --> 00:14:34,553
كَذَبَ سَعْد

199
00:14:34,577 --> 00:14:35,721
Sa'ad(سعد) lied.

200
00:14:36,116 --> 00:14:41,002
Now, the word, lie here, in this context means, is mistaken.

201
00:14:41,026 --> 00:14:45,351
It doesn't mean literally lie, it means that he is mistaken, Sa'ad(سعد) is mistaken.

202
00:14:45,808 --> 00:14:50,275
كَذَبَ سَعْد، وَلَكِنْ هَذَا يَوْم يُعَظِمُ الله فِيْهَ الْكَعْبَهْ

203
00:14:51,177 --> 00:14:55,261
Sa'ad(سَعد) has lied but this is a day in which Allah, will glorify Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

204
00:14:55,843 --> 00:14:58,077
The sanctity of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) will not be violated.

205
00:14:58,464 --> 00:15:03,392
And Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered that the banner be taken away from Saad Ibn Ubadah(سَعد اِبن عبادة)

206
00:15:03,568 --> 00:15:07,461
and be given to his son Qais Bin Saad Ibn Ubada(قيس بن سَعد اِبن عبادة).

207
00:15:07,669 --> 00:15:08,814
This is a for two reasons.

208
00:15:08,865 --> 00:15:15,427
The first reason, Rasool Allah ﷺ did not want Saad Ibn Ubadah(سَعد اِبن عبادة), to have authority

209
00:15:15,806 --> 00:15:19,233
and probably this would lead him into bloodshed into Makkah.

210
00:15:19,257 --> 00:15:23,795
You can see that Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to avoid shedding blood in Makkah.

211
00:15:24,070 --> 00:15:27,743
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ did not want the banner to remain in his hands,

212
00:15:27,783 --> 00:15:32,718
but in the same time Rasool Allah ﷺ did not want to anger or upset Saad Ibn Ubadah(سَعد اِبن عبادة).

213
00:15:32,894 --> 00:15:36,339
Saad Ibn Ubadah(سَعد اِبن عبادة) is gonna accept the orders of Rasool Ullah, no matter what?

214
00:15:36,538 --> 00:15:42,594
But probably there would be something in his heart, he might be upset that the banner was taken from him.

215
00:15:42,634 --> 00:15:45,251
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ gave it, to his own son.

216
00:15:45,802 --> 00:15:49,586
Rasool Allah ﷺ entered peacefully, there was no resistance.

217
00:15:50,098 --> 00:15:53,434
But the area in which Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) came in

218
00:15:53,735 --> 00:15:56,023
there was resistance from Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) and Hudail(حديل),

219
00:15:56,338 --> 00:15:59,361
Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) and Hudail(حديل) are tribes that live on the outskirts of Makkah,

220
00:15:59,402 --> 00:16:00,655
they don't live in Makkah itself.

221
00:16:01,214 --> 00:16:05,060
They put up a fight, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) just destroyed them.

222
00:16:05,478 --> 00:16:07,479
So, they, they all just ran away.

223
00:16:07,772 --> 00:16:11,233
They gave up and that was the end of resistance.

224
00:16:11,257 --> 00:16:13,819
Therefore, there's a difference of opinion among the scholars.

225
00:16:14,157 --> 00:16:16,831
هَلْ فُتِحَت الْمَكَةْ صُلْحًا اَمْ عُنْوَةً

226
00:16:17,188 --> 00:16:22,854
Was Makkah opened by force or was it opened through agreement?

227
00:16:23,085 --> 00:16:25,414
What are the implications of this difference of opinion?

228
00:16:25,438 --> 00:16:27,458
The implications are in matters of Fiqh(فقه),

229
00:16:27,610 --> 00:16:30,156
because when a land is opened by force

230
00:16:30,386 --> 00:16:36,875
than everything that belongs to the Kuffar(كفار) turns into the property of Muslims, even themselves.

231
00:16:37,243 --> 00:16:41,221
So, everything on the land and on top of the land becomes property of the Muslims.

232
00:16:41,405 --> 00:16:43,202
If that land was opened by force,

233
00:16:43,398 --> 00:16:48,938
so the population could be enslaved and all of their property could be taken away and split among the Muslims.

234
00:16:48,978 --> 00:16:50,856
 This is if, it was opened by force.

235
00:16:51,118 --> 00:16:54,526
However, if it was open, Sulhan(صلحا) , by agreement,

236
00:16:54,804 --> 00:16:58,342
then the Kuffar(كفار) can have some right of ownership

237
00:16:58,611 --> 00:17:01,493
and they are not enslaved and they remain free.

238
00:17:02,091 --> 00:17:06,705
So, there's a difference of opinion among Ulema(علماء) on Fateh Makkah(فتح مكه).

239
00:17:06,936 --> 00:17:10,667
Some scholars say it was opened by force and some of them say it was opened by agreement.

240
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:18,609
And the implications of this are the reflection of it is regarding the property that exists in Makkah.

241
00:17:19,021 --> 00:17:21,626
Rasool Allah ﷺ entered Makkah.

242
00:17:21,975 --> 00:17:26,705
Now, this is after an absence of eight years.

243
00:17:27,116 --> 00:17:34,229
Rasool Allah ﷺ has left Makkah eight years ago, secretly and there was a plot to kill him.

244
00:17:34,703 --> 00:17:39,115
And Rasool Allah ﷺ had to flee from the danger that existed in Makkah.

245
00:17:39,651 --> 00:17:43,270
Eight years and now Rasool Allah ﷺ is entering Makkah victoriously.

246
00:17:43,970 --> 00:17:48,705
Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Muhajiroon(مهاجرون) spent 13 years in Makkah suffering,

247
00:17:48,925 --> 00:17:56,937
torture, evil words, boycott, all types of harm that you could imagine the Muslims went through.

248
00:17:57,393 --> 00:17:59,475
And now it's chance for revenge.

249
00:17:59,834 --> 00:18:09,646
 It's a chance to slaughter those, who caused all of this punishment and torture and hardship on the Muslims.

250
00:18:10,118 --> 00:18:19,098
It could have been a chance for a great celebrations of victory, as different armies do,

251
00:18:19,453 --> 00:18:21,867
whenever they conquer a new land.

252
00:18:22,227 --> 00:18:25,701
But how did Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Muslims enter Makkah?

253
00:18:26,533 --> 00:18:39,270
Did Rasool Allah ﷺ enter Makkah with mission accomplished, propaganda and celebrations and puffing of champagne bottles as the Kuffar(كفار) do.?

254
00:18:39,484 --> 00:18:44,175
Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, when they entered into Makkah,

255
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:49,386
the description that was given of Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he was entering, is that

256
00:18:49,874 --> 00:18:55,522
he entered with humbleness, Khushooh(خشوع), and he was reciting Surah Fateh(سورة فتح).

257
00:18:56,362 --> 00:19:00,444
The Surah(سورة) of conquest and his head was lowered so down

258
00:19:00,748 --> 00:19:05,925
that it could touch the Rahal(رحل) of the camel, his beard was touching it

259
00:19:06,845 --> 00:19:09,865
and he would recite the Ayaat(آيات) and repeat them.

260
00:19:10,356 --> 00:19:16,251
He had the black turban on, and he had a white flag banner,

261
00:19:16,708 --> 00:19:20,596
and he entered into Makkah in a state of humbleness,

262
00:19:21,148 --> 00:19:28,180
thanking Allahعَزّوجَلّ for the conquest, praising Allahعَزّوجَلّ for what He has given him,

263
00:19:28,424 --> 00:19:31,477
Rasool Allah ﷺ then made Tawaaf(طواف) around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

264
00:19:31,958 --> 00:19:38,357
and then he called Uthman Bin Talha(عثمان بن طلحه), to bring the key of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

265
00:19:38,884 --> 00:19:42,866
The Key of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) belonged to Bannu Abd Daar(بنوعبد دار).

266
00:19:43,355 --> 00:19:48,116
Ka'ab(كعب), who's the great grandfather of Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he passed away,

267
00:19:48,331 --> 00:19:53,551
see all of the different honors of Makkah, were in his hand

268
00:19:53,797 --> 00:19:56,004
and then they were split among his children.

269
00:19:56,391 --> 00:20:04,966
So, the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ had the responsibility of providing water to the Hajjaj(حجاج).

270
00:20:05,337 --> 00:20:10,128
The well Zamzam(زمزم), they would provide the Hajjaj(حجاج) with water and that is called Sikaya(سقاية),

271
00:20:10,705 --> 00:20:14,184
and then the family have Bannu Abd Daar(بنوعبد دار),

272
00:20:14,208 --> 00:20:19,231
they were the custodians of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), they held on to the key, so the key was with them.

273
00:20:19,910 --> 00:20:24,194
Uthman(عثمان) was a Muslim and Rasool Allah ﷺ told him to go and get the key,

274
00:20:24,218 --> 00:20:25,487
the key was with his mother.

275
00:20:25,671 --> 00:20:28,672
So, he went in the beginning, she refused and then he took the key.

276
00:20:29,239 --> 00:20:31,120
And he brought it to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

277
00:20:31,339 --> 00:20:34,540
Rasool Allah ﷺ opened Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), and he entered

278
00:20:34,621 --> 00:20:39,584
and he saw a pigeon made out of wood, he destroyed it.

279
00:20:39,963 --> 00:20:47,250
There were images on the walls of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) of angels and Ibrahim عليه السّلام,

280
00:20:47,755 --> 00:20:51,555
using Istasqaam Bil Izlaam(إستسقام بلإزلام) which is the dividing arrows,

281
00:20:51,848 --> 00:20:54,428
which is one of the Bid'ah(بدعة) of Jahilliya(جاهلية).

282
00:20:54,819 --> 00:20:55,990
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

283
00:20:56,015 --> 00:20:56,985
قَاتَلَهُمُ الله

284
00:20:57,009 --> 00:20:57,978
May Allah Kill them.

285
00:20:58,349 --> 00:21:03,913
They portrayed our elder, meaning our grandfather, Ibrahim(ابراهيم),

286
00:21:04,293 --> 00:21:06,862
as using these divining arrows.

287
00:21:07,530 --> 00:21:15,030
And then he ordered Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) to wipe out all of these images from inside the Ka'aba(كعبه),

288
00:21:15,325 --> 00:21:21,359
so Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), soaked a cloth in water and then wiped out all of these images.

289
00:21:21,588 --> 00:21:25,294
So, when Rasool Allah ﷺ entered in Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), it was clean

290
00:21:25,673 --> 00:21:28,917
from all of the innovations of Jahilliya(جاهلية) and Kuffr(كفر).

291
00:21:29,111 --> 00:21:35,110
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ came out from Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) and he stood on the door of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), which was high,

292
00:21:35,373 --> 00:21:38,007
and by now all of the people were gathering around him.

293
00:21:38,512 --> 00:21:41,870
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ spoke to the crowd.

294
00:21:42,211 --> 00:21:47,611
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they all came out now to listen to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

295
00:21:48,107 --> 00:21:55,660
Let's go back a few years when Rasool Allah ﷺ received the initial revelation from Allahعَزّوجَلّ

296
00:21:55,985 --> 00:22:00,887
and was commanded to, deliver the warning to his people,

297
00:22:00,918 --> 00:22:02,834
وَأَنْذِرْ عَشِيرَتَكَ الْأَقْرَبِينَ

298
00:22:03,143 --> 00:22:07,469
Warn your close relatives or your clan, that was in the beginning.

299
00:22:07,598 --> 00:22:12,097
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ stood on a mountain in Makkah, and he said;

300
00:22:12,137 --> 00:22:12,938
 وَا صُباحَاه

301
00:22:13,374 --> 00:22:17,572
And this is the call to make when there is an emergency situation,

302
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:19,935
you don't just say Wa'sabahaa(وا صباحاه) for nothing,

303
00:22:19,959 --> 00:22:21,853
you say it when there's something very urgent

304
00:22:22,334 --> 00:22:25,779
because everybody is going to respond, it's a serious call.

305
00:22:26,432 --> 00:22:32,364
So all of the people came and those, who could not come sent a representative to listen.

306
00:22:32,759 --> 00:22:33,769
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

307
00:22:33,793 --> 00:22:37,092
إنِّي نَذِيرٌ لَكُمْ بيْنَ يَدَيْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمْ

308
00:22:37,448 --> 00:22:42,332
I'm delivering a warning to you, before a severe punishment will befall you.

309
00:22:42,610 --> 00:22:44,751
When Rasool Allah ﷺ said this, Abu Lahab(ابولهب) said;

310
00:22:44,775 --> 00:22:47,462
تَبًّا لَكْ ألهَذَا دَعَوْتَنَا

311
00:22:48,560 --> 00:22:52,269
May you be cut off, is this why you have summoned us?

312
00:22:52,830 --> 00:22:56,541
Abu Lahab(ابولهب) was buying and selling, a businessman

313
00:22:56,865 --> 00:23:00,910
and he left his shop and he came to listen to what Rasool Allah ﷺ had to say.

314
00:23:01,157 --> 00:23:04,097
And Rasool Allah ﷺ had this message to deliver to them,

315
00:23:04,137 --> 00:23:10,652
he was upset and angry and the crowds left and from that time on,

316
00:23:11,040 --> 00:23:15,907
no one wants to listen to  what, Rasool Allah ﷺ has to say.

317
00:23:16,763 --> 00:23:22,289
And imagine how difficult it is, to deliver Da'wah(دعوة) to people who don't want to listen.

318
00:23:22,662 --> 00:23:26,988
But now, since Rasool Allah ﷺ is leading an army,

319
00:23:27,649 --> 00:23:30,672
now since Rasool Allah ﷺ has strength,

320
00:23:30,801 --> 00:23:35,760
and since he is the head of state, everybody came voluntarily to listen.

321
00:23:36,155 --> 00:23:38,013
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not call anyone

322
00:23:38,259 --> 00:23:42,517
by the time Rasool Allah ﷺ came out and turned this back and face the people.

323
00:23:42,740 --> 00:23:49,961
All of the people of Makkah were under him listening to what Rasool Allah ﷺ has to say and watching his every move,

324
00:23:50,336 --> 00:23:55,172
because, when Rasool Allah ﷺ went to the well of Zamzam(زمزم), to drink from it and to make Wudhu(وضؤ).

325
00:23:55,412 --> 00:24:00,827
The Sahabah(صحابه) were rushing to grab the water that would drip from his body,

326
00:24:01,074 --> 00:24:03,369
and then they would wipe it over their skin.

327
00:24:03,759 --> 00:24:07,876
So, the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were saying: We have never seen such a king before.

328
00:24:08,739 --> 00:24:12,500
Now, they're watching every single movement of Rasool Ullah and they're reporting it,

329
00:24:12,543 --> 00:24:14,249
that's how we knew about this incident.

330
00:24:14,644 --> 00:24:16,522
It is because they reported it, to us.

331
00:24:16,745 --> 00:24:20,305
Rasool Allah ﷺ now, is the same Rasool Allah ﷺ then,

332
00:24:20,645 --> 00:24:26,186
but in the beginning because Rasool Allah ﷺ did not have strength.

333
00:24:26,210 --> 00:24:29,458
No one wanted to listen to what Rasool Allah ﷺ has to say.

334
00:24:29,498 --> 00:24:31,490
 But now, it is different.

335
00:24:31,605 --> 00:24:37,739
So Rasool Allah ﷺ delivered a short speech from the door of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

336
00:24:38,422 --> 00:24:44,769
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدالله), Praise be to Allah, Who has fulfilled His promise.

337
00:24:44,884 --> 00:24:47,118
صَدَقَه وَعْدَه  ونصره عبده

338
00:24:47,357 --> 00:24:48,870
And He has helped His servent.

339
00:24:49,616 --> 00:24:51,252
وَهَزَمَ الأَحْزَابَ وَحْدَةْ

340
00:24:51,577 --> 00:24:54,297
And He has defeated the opposing parties alone.

341
00:24:54,457 --> 00:24:59,320
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ is instituting some new laws in Makkah,

342
00:25:00,020 --> 00:25:08,972
compensation for those killed by kwazii intent by whip or cudgel shall be compensated by 100 camels,

343
00:25:09,226 --> 00:25:12,560
 this is Diyat Shib Al-Amd(دِيْة شِبْه أَلْعَمْدَ).

344
00:25:12,972 --> 00:25:23,752
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told them all privilege of ancestry and pride that existed in the Jahilliya(جاهلية) are finished.

345
00:25:24,353 --> 00:25:25,370
Listen to this statement;

346
00:25:25,601 --> 00:25:31,540
All privilege of ancestry and pride that existed in the Jahilliya(جاهلية) are finished.

347
00:25:32,139 --> 00:25:36,136
These are the foundations of the Society of Jahilliya(جاهلية).

348
00:25:36,507 --> 00:25:44,672
The foundation, the Constitution, the laws, the customs of the Arabs of Jahilliya(جاهلية) were based on this,

349
00:25:44,788 --> 00:25:46,683
privilege of ancestry and pride.

350
00:25:47,265 --> 00:25:48,729
In this one statement,

351
00:25:49,147 --> 00:25:56,054
Rasool Allah ﷺ is bringing a new era, and he's telling the people who are listening under his feet, he's telling him;

352
00:25:56,418 --> 00:26:01,852
That the time of Jahilliya(جاهلية), the rules of Jahilliya(جاهلية), the customs of Jahilliya(جاهلية),

353
00:26:02,097 --> 00:26:05,975
are all behind your backs now, they are all finished.

354
00:26:06,253 --> 00:26:08,663
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is bringing a new era,

355
00:26:08,910 --> 00:26:11,938
Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling the Kuffar(كفار), that Kuffr(كفر) is over with.

356
00:26:12,430 --> 00:26:15,799
I'm not going to accommodate you, I'm not going to accept your laws,

357
00:26:16,039 --> 00:26:19,049
I'm not going to accept your customs and ways, it's all finished.

358
00:26:19,451 --> 00:26:21,483
In another narration Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

359
00:26:21,761 --> 00:26:25,555
Both these factors meaning ancestry and pride are beneath these feet of mine.

360
00:26:26,208 --> 00:26:28,600
They're under my feet, they're over with.

361
00:26:29,471 --> 00:26:33,063
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not try to win over the hearts of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

362
00:26:33,087 --> 00:26:34,969
by accepting some of the rules and customs.

363
00:26:35,270 --> 00:26:39,319
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) would fight for their customers, they would die for their customs,

364
00:26:39,635 --> 00:26:43,276
who fought against Rasool Allah ﷺ for 20 years

365
00:26:43,764 --> 00:26:48,119
for no purpose other than the purpose of protecting the old way.

366
00:26:48,295 --> 00:26:50,152
They were not religious people by the way.

367
00:26:50,335 --> 00:26:54,459
Ya'ani(يعني) even though, they had 360 idols surrounding Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

368
00:26:54,483 --> 00:26:56,461
they were not known to be religious people.

369
00:26:57,457 --> 00:27:00,924
But it was the status quo that they were trying to protect.

370
00:27:01,225 --> 00:27:06,739
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not try to win them over by accepting some of Al-Jahilliya(ألجاهلية).

371
00:27:06,969 --> 00:27:15,256
Rasool Allah ﷺ in his first speech delivered in Makkah, made it clear that your ways are under my feet.

372
00:27:15,980 --> 00:27:19,191
Now, the key of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) is in the hands of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

373
00:27:19,216 --> 00:27:22,033
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), from the family of Bannu Hashim(بنوهاشم),

374
00:27:22,358 --> 00:27:23,446
he told Rasool Allah ﷺ;

375
00:27:23,470 --> 00:27:26,699
يَا رَسول الله، اِجْمَعْ لَنَا بَيْنَ سِقَايَة وَالْحِجَابَة

376
00:27:26,723 --> 00:27:32,122
O Rasool Ullah combined for us the honors of providing the pilgrims with water

377
00:27:32,389 --> 00:27:34,741
and holding on to the key of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

378
00:27:35,308 --> 00:27:36,990
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ do?

379
00:27:37,470 --> 00:27:41,735
And by the way, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said, this because it was a great opportunity.

380
00:27:41,809 --> 00:27:45,977
These were very important things to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

381
00:27:46,316 --> 00:27:49,953
I mean, holding onto the key of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) was such a great honor.

382
00:27:50,247 --> 00:27:55,061
In fact, that is what gave Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) this prestige, among all of the Arabs

383
00:27:55,085 --> 00:27:57,526
it was because they were custodians of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

384
00:27:57,898 --> 00:28:00,608
So, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was trying to convince Rasool Allah ﷺ,

385
00:28:00,632 --> 00:28:02,636
he took this opportunity and told Rasool Ullah;

386
00:28:02,922 --> 00:28:07,970
How about we combined for us for our family, the honor of holding onto the Key of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)?

387
00:28:08,034 --> 00:28:09,653
It's in your hands right now.

388
00:28:10,430 --> 00:28:14,525
Rasool Allah ﷺ called Uthman(عثمان) and he gave him the key, and they told him.

389
00:28:14,550 --> 00:28:18,694
خُذُوهَا خَالِدَةً مُخَلِّدَةً لَا يَاخُذْهَا مِنْكُمْ إِلَّا ظَالِمٌ

390
00:28:18,871 --> 00:28:23,131
Take it forever, and no one will take it from you but an oppressor,

391
00:28:23,526 --> 00:28:25,402
no one will take it from you but the tyrant

392
00:28:25,640 --> 00:28:32,159
and that is why the key of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) still exists among the descendants of Uthman Ibn Talha(عثمان ابن طلحه), until this day,

393
00:28:32,436 --> 00:28:33,892
and they are called Bannu Shaibah(بنوشيبة).

394
00:28:35,265 --> 00:28:39,522
The key has been passing on from father to son until, this day.

395
00:28:40,089 --> 00:28:45,445
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ riding on his camel, was going around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

396
00:28:45,769 --> 00:28:49,954
in one narration holding on to a stick and the other narration holding on to his bow,

397
00:28:50,271 --> 00:28:58,600
and he was pointing towards these idols, these glorified idols, these sacred idols, to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

398
00:28:58,640 --> 00:29:05,572
 and they're all watching and Rasool Allah ﷺ is going around, and he's poking these idols in their eyes.

399
00:29:06,048 --> 00:29:09,362
And in one narration, he was just pointing towards the idols,

400
00:29:09,515 --> 00:29:12,159
and they were falling one after the other.

401
00:29:12,311 --> 00:29:16,772
If he points towards the face of the idol, it would fall back on its back,

402
00:29:17,106 --> 00:29:22,106
and if Rasool Allah ﷺ points towards the back of the idol, it would fall on, on his face.

403
00:29:22,454 --> 00:29:27,946
And Rasool Allah ﷺ did that with the 360 idols surrounding Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

404
00:29:28,114 --> 00:29:31,991
and all of the Kuffar(كفار) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are watching this monumental moment,

405
00:29:32,503 --> 00:29:36,459
when all of their gods that have been there for centuries and centuries,

406
00:29:36,870 --> 00:29:40,667
they're watching their idols falling down breaking into pieces.

407
00:29:40,913 --> 00:29:42,700
Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying;

408
00:29:43,406 --> 00:29:47,337
وَقُلْ جَاءَ الْحَقُّ وَزَهَقَ الْبَاطِلُ ۚ إِنَّ الْبَاطِلَ كَانَ زَهُوقًا

409
00:29:47,576 --> 00:29:53,346
Rasool Allah ﷺ was reciting, this Ayah(آية), the truth has come, and error has gone.

410
00:29:53,607 --> 00:29:59,852
Error is bound to disappear, error or evil is bound to disappear

411
00:30:00,068 --> 00:30:02,267
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ told the people Quraish(قُرَيْشْ);

412
00:30:02,339 --> 00:30:03,957
مَا تَظُنُّوْنَ أَنِّي فَاعِلٌ بِكُمْ؟

413
00:30:04,423 --> 00:30:06,067
What do you think I will do to you?

414
00:30:06,751 --> 00:30:11,926
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they said: What they believe is the case with Muhammadﷺ

415
00:30:12,122 --> 00:30:12,863
they know him.

416
00:30:13,395 --> 00:30:15,702
قَالُوا: أَخٌ كَرِيمٌ، وَابْنُ أَخٍ كَرِيمٍ،

417
00:30:15,991 --> 00:30:20,456
They said: You are a noble brother and the son of a noble brother.

418
00:30:21,250 --> 00:30:22,583
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them;

419
00:30:22,799 --> 00:30:24,575
اِذْهَبُوا فَأَنْتُمْ الطُّلَقَاءُ

420
00:30:24,599 --> 00:30:26,921
Go! You are the freed ones.

421
00:30:28,097 --> 00:30:31,441
You are a Tulaqa'a(طلقاء), You are freed because you are in my hands.

422
00:30:31,953 --> 00:30:36,605
And I could, by a point of my finger by just waving my hand,

423
00:30:36,629 --> 00:30:39,264
I could order all of you to be executed.

424
00:30:39,681 --> 00:30:42,520
And that would happen, if I wanted to happen.

425
00:30:43,352 --> 00:30:44,655
But he told them you are free.

426
00:30:44,886 --> 00:30:51,391
And that's why the people who became Muslim, at the conquest of Makkah are called At-Tulaqa'a(اَطُّلقاء), the freed ones

427
00:30:51,511 --> 00:30:54,883
because Rasool Allah ﷺ is the one, who freed them, he released them.

428
00:30:54,939 --> 00:30:59,162
You are the released ones, probably the word released is more accurate.

429
00:30:59,408 --> 00:31:00,538
You are the released ones.

430
00:31:00,562 --> 00:31:02,351
اِذْهَبُوا فَأَنْتُمْ الطُّلَقَاءُ

431
00:31:02,604 --> 00:31:04,798
Go! You are the released ones.

432
00:31:05,060 --> 00:31:08,755
Rasool Allah ﷺ released them all but there was a blacklist.

433
00:31:09,461 --> 00:31:10,462
There were exceptions,

434
00:31:10,626 --> 00:31:13,637
this blacklist included the names of Abdullah bin Khattl(عبدالله بن خطل),

435
00:31:13,852 --> 00:31:17,055
Abdullah Bin Abi Sar'h(عبدالله بن ابي ألسرح), Maqees Bin Sababah(مقيس بن صبابة),

436
00:31:17,363 --> 00:31:21,768
Al-Huwairis Bin Naqeez(الحويرث بن نقيذ) and Sarah(سارة), Fartana(فرتنى) and Arnub(ارنب).

437
00:31:22,951 --> 00:31:28,524
So, there were four men and three women, Rasool Allah ﷺ said, about these,

438
00:31:28,786 --> 00:31:32,829
اُقْتُلُوْهُمْ وَلو وَجَدْتُمُوْهُمْ مُعَلَقِيْنَ بِأَسْتَارِ الْكَعْبَةِ

439
00:31:32,884 --> 00:31:38,910
Execute them, even if you see them, hanging on to the clothes of Al-Ka'aba(الكعبه).

440
00:31:39,633 --> 00:31:43,600
Why were these excluded from the rest of the people of Makkah?

441
00:31:44,010 --> 00:31:47,622
With Abdullah Bin Khattl(عبدالله بن خطل), he became Muslim, he made Hijra(هجرة)

442
00:31:48,016 --> 00:31:52,090
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ sent him to collect Sadaqah(صدقه), charity.

443
00:31:52,624 --> 00:31:57,355
On the way, Ya'ani(يعني) he was sent with a man from Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار) and then he had a servant, a slave

444
00:31:57,649 --> 00:32:00,884
on the way he was upset with his servant,

445
00:32:01,021 --> 00:32:04,881
it says in one narration, that he ordered the servant to prepare lunch.

446
00:32:05,182 --> 00:32:09,628
And when it was time for lunch, he told him, where's the lunch the servant told them I forgot.

447
00:32:09,859 --> 00:32:10,608
So, he killed him.

448
00:32:11,190 --> 00:32:13,361
Now, he knew that is going to be punished for this,

449
00:32:13,601 --> 00:32:17,959
Rasool Allah ﷺ was not gonna let him go, in Islam, there's justice,

450
00:32:18,346 --> 00:32:23,733
whether you are a slave or a noble man, the law of Allah will apply to you.

451
00:32:24,011 --> 00:32:26,218
So, Abdullah Bin Khattl(عبدالله بن خطل), knew this in advance.

452
00:32:26,730 --> 00:32:31,504
He therefore, decided to run away to Makkah and he committed apostasy.

453
00:32:31,906 --> 00:32:39,840
And he had two slave girls, whom he would teach to sing against Rasool Allah ﷺ.

454
00:32:40,173 --> 00:32:43,793
So, Abdullah bin Khattl(عبدالله بن خطل), he was excluded because of his Riddah(ردة)

455
00:32:43,818 --> 00:32:46,269
and because of his blasphemy against Rasool Allah ﷺ.

456
00:32:46,796 --> 00:32:51,023
And his two slave girls, singers Fartana(فرتنى) and Arnub(ارنب).

457
00:32:51,496 --> 00:32:57,796
They were included on the list because of their blasphemy against Rasool Allah ﷺ, cursing Rasool Ullah.

458
00:32:58,275 --> 00:33:00,658
Abdullah Bin Abi Sar'h(عبدالله بن ابي السرح), he became Muslim

459
00:33:00,682 --> 00:33:05,580
and he would write Qur'an for Rasool Allah ﷺ,

460
00:33:05,604 --> 00:33:10,042
Rasool Allah ﷺ had scribes, he would recite the Ayaat(آيات) to them

461
00:33:10,066 --> 00:33:12,141
and they would write them down.

462
00:33:12,387 --> 00:33:19,012
Abdullah Bin Abi Sar'h(عبدالله بن ابي سرح), he then ran away and he became a Murtadd(مرتد), he became an apostate.

463
00:33:19,290 --> 00:33:23,890
And he went as far as telling the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

464
00:33:24,245 --> 00:33:26,684
that I would change Qur'an, when I would write it down,

465
00:33:26,708 --> 00:33:28,603
I would change the meanings of Qur'an.

466
00:33:29,240 --> 00:33:30,443
Maqees Bin Sababah(مقيس بن صبابة),

467
00:33:30,768 --> 00:33:36,498
Maqees Bin Sababah(مقيس بن صبابة), his brother was a Muslim in the Battle of Bannu Al-Mustallaq(بنوالمصطلق),

468
00:33:36,759 --> 00:33:42,004
he was killed by mistake he was killed by mistake by a man from Al-Ansaar(الانصار).

469
00:33:42,868 --> 00:33:47,914
So, Maqees(مقيس), he made Hijrah(هجرة) and he became Muslim.

470
00:33:48,441 --> 00:33:51,876
Just to collect the money, the blood money of his brother.

471
00:33:52,191 --> 00:33:53,445
So, Rasool Ullah paid him the money.

472
00:33:53,485 --> 00:33:56,707
After he received the money he ran away and became a Murtadd(مرتد).

473
00:33:57,599 --> 00:33:59,046
Al-Huwairis Bin Naqeez(الحويرس بن نقيظ);

474
00:33:59,300 --> 00:34:06,386
When Al-Abbas Ibn Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبد المطلب) sent Fatima(فاطمه) and Zainab(زينب), the daughters of Rasool Allah ﷺ to Madina.

475
00:34:06,878 --> 00:34:12,529
Al-Huwairis(الحويرث), he provoked the camel, which Zainab(زينب) and Fatimah(فاطمه) were on,

476
00:34:12,693 --> 00:34:16,019
and that led to both of them falling.

477
00:34:16,727 --> 00:34:19,445
And Zainab(زينب) having a miscarriage.

478
00:34:20,223 --> 00:34:25,112
The daughter of Rasool Allah ﷺ had a miscarriage because of the actions of this man, Al-Huwairis(الحويرث).

479
00:34:25,567 --> 00:34:31,999
Sarah(سارة) was a slave girl, that belonged to someone in Makkah,

480
00:34:32,023 --> 00:34:34,627
and she used to sing against Rasool Allah ﷺ.

481
00:34:34,651 --> 00:34:37,265
So, we can see that everyone on this blacklist

482
00:34:38,018 --> 00:34:42,957
was excluded from the forgiveness of Rasool Allah ﷺ

483
00:34:43,504 --> 00:34:46,110
for one, of two reasons,

484
00:34:46,644 --> 00:34:51,185
either because they have committed Riddah(ردا), apostasy or because of blasphemy.

485
00:34:51,641 --> 00:34:55,315
These are the two things that are unforgiven, Riddah(ردة)

486
00:34:55,672 --> 00:35:03,656
and speaking in an insulting way, against Rasool Allah ﷺ there's no forgiveness for both of these two crimes.

487
00:35:04,206 --> 00:35:05,658
And that's why Ibn Taymiyyah(إبن تيميه) says;

488
00:35:05,841 --> 00:35:13,040
That the rules concerning Riddah(ردة), apostasy are more strict than the rules, concerning Kuffr(كفر).

489
00:35:13,177 --> 00:35:19,755
One example a kafir(كافر) who is prisoner of war, the Imam(امام) has a right to execute him,

490
00:35:20,267 --> 00:35:29,935
or to free him, or to ask for ransom, or to exchange him with Muslim prisoners of war or to enslave him.

491
00:35:30,604 --> 00:35:33,898
It is up to the Imam(امام) to choose one of these options.

492
00:35:34,312 --> 00:35:35,521
However, with the Murtadd(مرتد),

493
00:35:35,545 --> 00:35:39,646
Ibn Taymiyyah(إبن تيميه) says; There's only one option and that is to be executed.

494
00:35:40,227 --> 00:35:42,486
A Murtadd(مرتد) prisoner of war

495
00:35:42,785 --> 00:35:48,951
cannot be freed, cannot be enslaved, cannot be exchanged, he can only be executed,

496
00:35:49,690 --> 00:35:53,704
or if he becomes Muslim, then he is freed.

497
00:35:53,832 --> 00:35:58,871
But if he refuses, then there's only have the option of execution.

498
00:35:59,478 --> 00:36:05,946
That's one example of how the rulings concerning apostasy are different than the rulings concerning Kuffr(كفر).

499
00:36:06,340 --> 00:36:11,599
Abdullah bin Khattl(عبدالله بن خطل) was seen hanging on to the clothes of Al-Ka'aba(الكعبه)

500
00:36:11,775 --> 00:36:14,268
and he was executed on the spot.

501
00:36:14,632 --> 00:36:16,862
Some narrations say that Fartana(فرطنى) was killed

502
00:36:17,140 --> 00:36:21,844
while Arnub(ارنب) she became Muslim and she was forgiven.

503
00:36:22,113 --> 00:36:30,681
Abdullah Bin Abi Sar'h(عبدالله بن ابي سرح), he sought refuge with his brother from breastfeeding Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان), Akhoo Min-Ar-Ridha(أخوه من الرضاعة)

504
00:36:31,221 --> 00:36:36,586
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) took, Abdullah Bin Abi Sar'h(عبدالله بن ابي سرح) to Rasool Allah ﷺ

505
00:36:37,078 --> 00:36:38,597
and Abdullah Bin Abi Sar'h(عبدالله بن ابي سرح) said;

506
00:36:38,921 --> 00:36:42,163
I came to give you a Baiyah(بيعة), Rasool Ullah was quite,

507
00:36:42,898 --> 00:36:46,634
he said: I came to give you Baiyah(بيعة) Rasool Ullah did not respond.

508
00:36:47,184 --> 00:36:50,742
The third time he said: I came to give you Baiyah(بيعة).

509
00:36:50,992 --> 00:36:53,167
Rasool Allah ﷺ accepted his Baiyah(بيعة).

510
00:36:53,365 --> 00:36:57,520
And then when he left, Rasool Allah ﷺ told the men, who were there.

511
00:36:58,133 --> 00:37:03,025
Is there no wise men among you, who could have got up and killed him?

512
00:37:03,279 --> 00:37:06,112
When you saw I was remaining silent.

513
00:37:06,850 --> 00:37:12,179
So, the Ansaar(انصار) said: But O Rasool Ullah could you not have given us some signal?

514
00:37:12,507 --> 00:37:13,807
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

515
00:37:14,225 --> 00:37:17,589
مَا يَنْبَغِيْ لِنَبِيٍّ اَنْ يَقْتُلَ بِالْاِشَارَةْ

516
00:37:17,827 --> 00:37:20,735
Prophets do not kill by making signals.

517
00:37:21,584 --> 00:37:25,981
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: It's not appropriate for me, as a prophet to give you a signal.

518
00:37:26,413 --> 00:37:30,958
You already knew my Hukum(حكم) my ruling concerning him, so you could have killed him.

519
00:37:31,266 --> 00:37:34,856
It says in one narration that one of the Ansaar(انصار) already had his hand on the sword.

520
00:37:35,250 --> 00:37:40,022
He was ready to execute the man but he was waiting for a signal from Rasool Allah ﷺ.

521
00:37:40,300 --> 00:37:45,098
Subhan Allah(سبحان الله), that was the Qadar(قدر) of Allah to spare the life of Abdullah Bin Abi Sar'h(عبدالله بن ابي سرح),

522
00:37:45,303 --> 00:37:47,293
because he became a good Muslim after that.

523
00:37:47,531 --> 00:37:52,030
In fact, it says that he died in Sujood(سجود) of Salat Ul Fajr(صلاةالفجر)

524
00:37:52,370 --> 00:37:59,717
and he held some very high positions of authority in the times of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and Uthman(عثمان).

525
00:38:00,390 --> 00:38:04,003
Maqees Bin Sababah(مقيس بن صبابه) was killed by his cousin,

526
00:38:04,398 --> 00:38:06,797
Al-Huwairis Bin Naqeez(الحويرث بن نقيذ) was also killed.

527
00:38:07,169 --> 00:38:10,551
Sarah(سارة) some say that she was forgiven.

528
00:38:11,131 --> 00:38:16,974
So, we can see the important ruling here of the Hukum(حكم) of Sabb(صب) of Rasool Allah ﷺ do.

529
00:38:16,998 --> 00:38:20,770
The ruling of committing blasphemy against Rasool Allah ﷺ.

530
00:38:21,335 --> 00:38:28,646
Umma Haana(اُمّ هاني) is the sister of Ali Ibn Abi Talib,  رضي الله عنهم اجمعين,

531
00:38:28,733 --> 00:38:32,670
two her in laws, sought refuge with her.

532
00:38:32,987 --> 00:38:35,367
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) came in and said: I will kill them,

533
00:38:35,965 --> 00:38:40,956
Umma Haana(اُمّ هاني) had them hide in her place and then she went to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

534
00:38:41,163 --> 00:38:45,401
who was bathing and Fatimah رضي الله عنه was screening him.

535
00:38:45,433 --> 00:38:50,247
and he was bathing from out of the container that's still had marks of dough in it.

536
00:38:50,517 --> 00:38:56,972
Rasool Allah ﷺ welcomed her and greeted her and said: What has brought you.?

537
00:38:57,219 --> 00:39:00,148
He greeted her very well and then he said: What has brought you.?

538
00:39:00,340 --> 00:39:02,486
She said: The son of my mother,

539
00:39:02,615 --> 00:39:07,379
has said that he will kill the two men that I have given protection.

540
00:39:07,637 --> 00:39:08,696
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

541
00:39:09,124 --> 00:39:11,104
 أَجَرْنَا مَنْ أَجَرْتِ يَا أمَّ هَانَئ

542
00:39:11,405 --> 00:39:15,699
We give protection to the ones, you have given protection, Umma Haana(اُمّ هاني).

543
00:39:16,063 --> 00:39:22,268
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ approved her protection, and he has spared the lives of her two in laws.

544
00:39:22,750 --> 00:39:27,002
And Umma Haana(اُمّ هاني) saw Rasool Allah ﷺ pray eight Raka'at(ركعات),

545
00:39:27,365 --> 00:39:29,145
every two Raka'a(ركعة) were separate.

546
00:39:29,336 --> 00:39:31,215
So, the scholars had the difference of opinion.

547
00:39:31,703 --> 00:39:35,386
Or these are Salaat-Uz-Zuhaa(صلاة الضحى) or are they the Salah(صلاة) of conquest.

548
00:39:35,585 --> 00:39:37,927
Some of them said: It is the (صلاة) of conquest,

549
00:39:38,221 --> 00:39:45,313
because no one has reported them except Umma Haana(اُمّ هاني) in this particular day, which was the day of the opening of Makkah.

550
00:39:46,121 --> 00:39:47,281
While some of them say

551
00:39:47,597 --> 00:39:50,457
that they are Salaat Uz Zuhaa(صلاة الضحى) because in the narration it says

552
00:39:50,725 --> 00:39:52,648
that he prayed them in the time of the Dhuhaa(الضحى).

553
00:39:53,129 --> 00:39:55,406
Abu Qahafah(ابوقحافة), the Father of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

554
00:39:55,840 --> 00:40:02,037
He told his youngest daughter to take him on top of the mountain of Abu Qubais(ابوقبيس).

555
00:40:02,261 --> 00:40:03,513
This is a mountain in Makkah.

556
00:40:03,978 --> 00:40:05,406
And his sight was very weak.

557
00:40:05,568 --> 00:40:07,798
 So, she took him on top of the mountain.

558
00:40:08,091 --> 00:40:10,875
He told her: O daughter describe to me what you see?

559
00:40:11,187 --> 00:40:11,426
She said;

560
00:40:11,451 --> 00:40:12,408
  اِنِّيْ اَرَآء سَوَادً

561
00:40:12,447 --> 00:40:13,664
I see a black mass.

562
00:40:14,160 --> 00:40:19,388
He told her, those are the horsemen and then he told her what do you see?

563
00:40:19,412 --> 00:40:21,932
she said: I see a man going back and fro.

564
00:40:22,655 --> 00:40:24,602
So, Abu Qahafah(ابوقحافة) said;

565
00:40:24,626 --> 00:40:25,506
ذَالِكَ الْوَازَة

566
00:40:25,848 --> 00:40:30,196
That is the man, who gives instructions to the cavalry.

567
00:40:30,870 --> 00:40:34,486
And then she said: I see the black mass dispersing.

568
00:40:34,881 --> 00:40:39,909
He said: The orders have been given to the cavalry. Let's rush back.

569
00:40:40,510 --> 00:40:45,748
But they didn't get home on time, they met the cavalry on their way.

570
00:40:46,095 --> 00:40:53,781
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), one of the soldiers saw a silver necklace on the neck of the Daughter of Abu Qahafah(ابوقحافة).

571
00:40:54,031 --> 00:40:56,227
So, he ripped it apart from her neck.

572
00:40:56,630 --> 00:41:01,639
Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه went to his father and he brought him to meet Rasool Ullah.

573
00:41:02,322 --> 00:41:04,430
When Rasool Allah ﷺ saw the old man.

574
00:41:04,892 --> 00:41:06,669
Rasool Ullah told Abu Bakr(ابو بكر);

575
00:41:06,906 --> 00:41:09,897
هَلَّا تَرَكْتَ الشَيْخْ فَاَكُوْنُ اَنَا الَّذِيْ آتِيْكْ

576
00:41:10,237 --> 00:41:11,970
Why didn't you leave the Shaikh(شيخ),

577
00:41:12,133 --> 00:41:14,347
Shaikh(شيخ) means old man at home,

578
00:41:14,483 --> 00:41:18,375
so that I would be the one, who would come to him. Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said;

579
00:41:18,852 --> 00:41:22,831
هُوَ اَحَقّ اَنْ يَمْشِيْ اَلَيْكْ مِنْ اَنْ تَمْشِيَّ اَنْتَ اِلَيْه

580
00:41:23,174 --> 00:41:28,519
It is more fitting for him to come to you rather than you go to him.

581
00:41:28,551 --> 00:41:35,122
So, this shows you the respect that Rasool Allah ﷺ had for Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) in offering to go and visit his father.

582
00:41:35,319 --> 00:41:39,551
And you can see the respect, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) had for Rasool Allah ﷺ,

583
00:41:39,729 --> 00:41:43,938
telling Rasool Ullah that my father should come to you, not you go to him.

584
00:41:44,402 --> 00:41:48,152
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ put his hand on the chest of Abu Qahafah(ابوقحافة).

585
00:41:48,473 --> 00:41:52,314
And he wiped his chest and said: Aslim(أسْلِم) so he became Muslim.

586
00:41:52,513 --> 00:41:56,734
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told them: To change the color of his hair because

587
00:41:57,049 --> 00:41:59,961
his hair was described as being like Sughama(ثغامة),

588
00:42:00,081 --> 00:42:01,450
Sughama(ثغامة) is a white bird.

589
00:42:01,525 --> 00:42:04,201
So, all of his hair was gray, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

590
00:42:04,225 --> 00:42:06,412
غَيَّرُه’ وَلَا تُقَرِّبُوْه’ السوَادْ

591
00:42:06,705 --> 00:42:09,164
change the color of his hair, but don't make it black.

592
00:42:09,481 --> 00:42:16,059
Therefore, the Ulema(علماء) have derived the ruling that the old man should not dye his hair black,

593
00:42:16,853 --> 00:42:21,218
but you change it to a different color and that is the color of Hinnah(حنا), which is red.

594
00:42:22,082 --> 00:42:27,808
And some scholars said, that if a person is young, then they can dye their hair black.

595
00:42:28,274 --> 00:42:32,896
But if they are at the age, which is natural for them to have gray hair,

596
00:42:33,174 --> 00:42:36,692
they shouldn't dye it black, but they should dye it with Hinnah(حنا).

597
00:42:37,852 --> 00:42:40,779
The daughter of Abu Qahafah(ابو قحافة), the sister of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

598
00:42:41,334 --> 00:42:44,742
she told her brother, that her necklace was taken away.

599
00:42:44,933 --> 00:42:46,337
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said;

600
00:42:46,387 --> 00:42:47,305
 اَيُّهَاالنَّاس

601
00:42:47,351 --> 00:42:53,435
O people, has anyone taken the necklace of my sister, no one responded.

602
00:42:53,705 --> 00:42:54,297
So he said;

603
00:42:54,354 --> 00:42:55,227
  إِحتَسِبِيْ

604
00:42:55,331 --> 00:42:59,923
He told her to seek the Ajr(أجر) of it from Allah.

605
00:43:00,287 --> 00:43:04,344
  إِحتَسِبِيْ يَا بُنَيَّ فَاِنَّ الْاَمَانَة فِيْ النَّاسِ يَوْمَ قَلِيْلْ

606
00:43:04,469 --> 00:43:08,607
Because trust is little in the people today.

607
00:43:08,942 --> 00:43:10,794
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) comments on this and says;

608
00:43:10,834 --> 00:43:15,147
The reason why Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said this is because the army was large.

609
00:43:15,732 --> 00:43:21,403
And Ibn Kathir(ابن كثير) he is finding an excuse for whoever took the necklace.

610
00:43:22,062 --> 00:43:26,820
He said: Probably he took it considering that it belongs to the people of war.

611
00:43:27,551 --> 00:43:29,787
So, what belongs to them is Ghaneemah(غنيمة)

612
00:43:29,994 --> 00:43:33,248
and he's also given excuse to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

613
00:43:33,698 --> 00:43:38,420
when he said that the trust today is very rare among the people,

614
00:43:38,784 --> 00:43:43,060
meaning that particular day and not in that era or time,

615
00:43:43,393 --> 00:43:48,568
that particular day because it's a large army, and things could get out of hand,

616
00:43:48,830 --> 00:43:54,394
when an army enters into a town and you have a lot of soldiers.

617
00:43:54,750 --> 00:43:56,933
These are things that happened with armies.

618
00:43:57,266 --> 00:44:00,150
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was referring to that particular day

619
00:44:00,381 --> 00:44:02,361
and was not referring to the people in general.

620
00:44:03,770 --> 00:44:07,258
In Al-Bukhari(ألبخاري) it says that Usama Bin Zaid(اسامه بن زيد) asked Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

621
00:44:07,283 --> 00:44:08,117
اَيْنَ الْمَنْزِل غَدًا

622
00:44:08,141 --> 00:44:09,618
Where are you going to spend the night?

623
00:44:10,185 --> 00:44:11,328
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

624
00:44:11,352 --> 00:44:13,413
وَهَلْ تَرَكَ لَنَا عَقِيْلٌ مِنْ الرَّبَا

625
00:44:13,437 --> 00:44:15,914
Did Aqeel(عقيل) leave for us any property?

626
00:44:15,954 --> 00:44:18,149
Aqeel(عقيل) has taken over all of the inheritance.

627
00:44:18,289 --> 00:44:21,492
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ had nothing left, and then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

628
00:44:21,621 --> 00:44:24,218
لَا يَرِثُ الْمُؤمِن الْكَافِر وَالْكَافِرِ الْمُؤمِنْ

629
00:44:24,473 --> 00:44:27,511
The believer does not inherit from the disbelievers

630
00:44:27,535 --> 00:44:30,352
and the disbelievers does not inherit from the believer.

631
00:44:30,614 --> 00:44:33,851
And this is the Hukum(حكم) and ruling regarding inheritance.

632
00:44:34,292 --> 00:44:37,271
There is no inheritance between two different religions.

633
00:44:37,786 --> 00:44:40,213
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said and this is in Bukhari(البخاري);

634
00:44:40,460 --> 00:44:45,154
مَنْزِلُنَا غَدً اِنْ شَاءَالله بِخَيْفِ بَنِيْ كَنَانَهْ حَيْثُ تَقَاسَمُ عَلَى اَلْكُفْرْ

635
00:44:45,503 --> 00:44:47,670
Tomorrow we're going to stay we're going to spend the night

636
00:44:48,020 --> 00:44:52,703
In Sha Allah(انشاءالله) by the will of Allah in Khaef Bani Kananah(خيف بني كنانة),

637
00:44:53,160 --> 00:44:57,291
place where they have vowed on disbelief.

638
00:44:57,787 --> 00:45:01,284
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ wants to replace the Kuffr(كفر) that happened in that place

639
00:45:01,593 --> 00:45:05,966
by spending the night there and reviving the spirit of Eeman(ايمان)

640
00:45:06,267 --> 00:45:08,777
or bringing the spirit of Eeman(ايمان) into that place.

641
00:45:08,922 --> 00:45:12,931
So, if evil happened in that place, he will bring good to it.

642
00:45:14,077 --> 00:45:17,936
These are some events that happened during Fateh Makkah(فتح مكه).

643
00:45:18,401 --> 00:45:22,983
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًاكَثِيْرَا

644
00:45:23,288 --> 00:45:25,635
وَالسلا م عليكم ورحمة الله  وبركاته

